<!-- claude-context-kit seed rules.
     Merge into ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md with:  ./install.sh --seed
     Each "- " bullet is one rule; only bullets are merged, and a rule is
     matched by its content, not by this heading. Rules the target already
     has, verbatim or reworded, are reported and left alone.
     These are project-agnostic. Nothing here names a language, company, or repo. -->

## Working rules

- Ground every progress claim in a tool result from this session. Report only
  work you can point to. If something is unverified, say so. Never present an
  inferred result as a measured one.
- A check that returns zero is only evidence if it could have returned
  non-zero. Verify by decoding or transforming the candidate data, not by
  matching an expected pattern.
- Verify the shipped artifact against its source, never against itself. An exit
  code is not verification.
- Reviews and audits run their specialist and adversarial subagents. Spawning
  them is expected and does not need permission each time. A model reviewing
  code it just wrote is marking its own homework.
- Never pass a secret as a command-line argument. It lands in argv, in shell
  history, and in system logs. Use an interactive prompt, an env file, or stdin.
- Never construct a delete path from unvalidated variables. Assert every
  component is non-empty and assert the resolved path sits under an expected
  root, or do not delete.
- Never run a service's own tooling as a different user than the service runs
  as. It rewrites config ownership and breaks the service.
- A finding that produces a silent wrong outcome — wrong data, wrong file, no
  error raised — gets fixed or filed. Never deferred as "worth watching."
- Check acceptance criteria against downstream work, not only the current task.
  A criterion can be correct in isolation and inoperable against the next change.
- File findings the moment they are found. Anything left only in a conversation
  is lost when the session ends.
- Point project context at a live tracker, never at a document. Documents go
  stale silently, and a superseded spec is worse than no spec.
- Runs are autonomous by default. Stop only for physical devices, credentials,
  or consequential or irreversible choices. Otherwise take your own
  recommendation and keep moving, reporting decisions as you go.
